From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matteo Melli <matteom@ongres.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strip self-referential symlinks after download

Some GitHub tarballs include a "_codeql_detected_source_root" symlink
that points to "." (the package root). Bazel's glob(["**"]) evaluation
over the downloaded source tree then fails with:

  ERROR: infinite symlink expansion detected

and patches applied via rctx.patch can't even be read through the
symlink (it resolves to a directory). Delete any "-> ." symlinks right
after extraction so both the glob and subsequent patch application
behave.
---
 download/archives/repository.bzl | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/download/archives/repository.bzl b/download/archives/repository.bzl
--- a/download/archives/repository.bzl
+++ b/download/archives/repository.bzl
@@ -664,6 +664,15 @@ def _impl(rctx):
                 failed_downloads[version].append(version)
                 continue
 
+            # Some GitHub tarballs (CodeQL-enabled repos) include a
+            # "_codeql_detected_source_root" symlink pointing to "."
+            # which makes glob(["**"]) loop and also breaks rctx.patch.
+            # Strip any symlink whose target is literally ".".
+            rctx.execute(
+                ["find", repo_path, "-type", "l", "-lname", ".", "-delete"],
+                quiet = True,
+            )
+
             if "integrity" not in repo.context:
                 msg = "{}/{}: WARNING: integrity missing. "
                 msg += "Please add the integrity / sha256 to the index: {} / {}"
-- 
